Port beast-splitter v11.1 off the Boost.Asio APIs removed in Boost 1.87.

Applied by the Dockerfile only when the source still uses io_service and the
installed Boost no longer provides it (Debian forky and later). Every
replacement exists since Boost 1.66:

- io_service -> io_context
- steady_timer::expires_from_now() -> expires_after()
- io_context::post() -> boost::asio::post()
- resolver::query / resolver::iterator -> resolve(host, service) / results_type
- no longer link -lboost_system (header-only since Boost 1.69, removed in 1.89)

Remove this patch once a beast-splitter release no longer uses io_service.

